{
  "comment": [
    "Regeneration (feature 0004 T11). The runner reads one vector per file (ADR 0045), so each entry's 'file' member names its output under conformance/vectors/jwt/positive/; it is not a vector member and is dropped when splitting.",
    "1. node conformance/tools/jwt-oracle/gen.mjs conformance/tools/jwt-oracle/specs/positive.json <tmp>/positive.json",
    "2. node -e 'const fs=require(\"fs\");const o=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(process.argv[1]));for(const v of o.vectors){const f=v.file;delete v.file;fs.writeFileSync(\"conformance/vectors/jwt/positive/\"+f,JSON.stringify(v,null,2)+\"\\n\")}' <tmp>/positive.json",
    "HS*, EdDSA and Ed25519 output is deterministic and re-runs byte for byte; ES* signatures are randomized, so a re-run rewrites those files with different, equally valid tokens: regenerate them only on purpose.",
    "Expected verdicts are written by hand here (the oracle never decides them); jwt.issue round trips and the RFC 7515 A.2 entry build no token and pass through."
  ],
  "vectors": [
    {
